  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Riviera Vet, on route du Plan de la Tour in Sainte-Maxime, is organised into two entities — RivieraDOG for dogs and RivieraCAT for cats — and specialises in the pet passports and deworming treatments needed to travel with your dog to the United Kingdom. Well rated (4.7/5 from 197 Google reviews).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>If you're preparing a trip to the United Kingdom with your dog, the paperwork (European pet passport, deworming treatment within the required window) needs to be planned ahead: this vet practice is well versed in these formalities. As a reminder, the general rule verified with the French national veterinary board (Ordre national des vétérinaires) and brexit.gouv.fr: the praziquantel-based deworming treatment must be given between 24h and 120h (5 days) before entering the United Kingdom, and recorded in section VII of the European pet passport. Open Monday to Friday from 9am to 7pm and Saturday from 9am to 5pm.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the deworming window before travelling to the United Kingdom is strict (between 24h and 5 days before entry) — book far enough in advance.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Sainte-Maxime and its seafront are close by.</p>
